# ── line endings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Normalize text to LF in the repo; shell scripts MUST stay LF on checkout
# (a CRLF .sh breaks MSYS bash on the Windows release job and Windows
# clones with autocrlf).  Binary assets are marked so autocrlf never
# touches them.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/* text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ttf binary

# ── public-export exclusions ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paths excluded from any public export (`git archive` / mirror publish):
# internal docs, the project-local agent config, and the private-origin
# CI workflows (inert on GitHub, but noise + infra disclosure) — none
# ship in a public release.
docs/internal/ export-ignore
docs/internal/** export-ignore
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
# The pre-push CI-status hook is private-origin only: it reports gitea
# Actions verdicts for workflows that are themselves export-ignored, and
# its default token path is the owner's.  commit-msg DOES ship — that one
# enforces a policy any contributor is held to.
scripts/hooks/pre-push export-ignore
# Owner-device debug tools (arm/disarm a KNULLI TrimUI for a debug session):
# they default to the owner's LAN address, embed the firmware's default root
# password for sshpass, edit /boot on the device, and point at the internal
# runbooks.  Internal tooling, like docs/internal — caught by the 0.9.7 cut's
# gate b (private-refs grep).
scripts/trimui_arm_debug.sh export-ignore
scripts/trimui_disarm_debug.sh export-ignore
# Owner rulings, 2026-09-15 (the 0.9.7 cut): the winget manifests were
# prepared for 0.9.6 and never submitted — stale public URLs if shipped; and
# the preview-clip script makes clips WITH the game's audio, for the owner's
# own devices only (no clip with audio goes to GitHub, and neither does the
# tool whose purpose that is).
packaging/winget/ export-ignore
packaging/winget/** export-ignore
scripts/make_preview_clip.sh export-ignore
.gitea/ export-ignore
.gitea/** export-ignore
